# slobodankovacevic.com

This repo contains a Jekyll-based personal site.

## Run locally

This project is intended to run locally with `docker compose`. Rancher Desktop and Docker Desktop both work as Docker-compatible runtimes.

### Prerequisites

- A running Docker-compatible daemon such as Rancher Desktop or Docker Desktop
- Port `4000` available on your machine

### Start the site

```sh
docker compose up
```

Open [http://localhost:4000](http://localhost:4000).

On the first run, startup can take longer because Docker may need to pull the `jekyll/jekyll:latest` image and Bundler will install gems into the container volume.

### Live reload

Jekyll runs in watch mode, so local content changes are rebuilt automatically while `docker compose up` is running.

### Stop the site

```sh
docker compose down
```

## Troubleshooting

- If `docker compose` cannot connect to the daemon, start Rancher Desktop or Docker Desktop first.
- If startup gets stuck after dependency changes, reset the container volume and try again:

```sh
docker compose down -v
docker compose up
```
